# S11.2-R14 probe invocation binding — 2026-09-23

Status: `STOPPED_SAFE_CONTROLLER_CONTRACT_RED`

## Observed result

- The backup-first controller completed the source/runtime backup and installed
  the frozen technical-latency probe unit.
- The first and only probe process completed successfully (`Result=success`,
  `ExecMainStatus=0`).
- The unit journal contains exactly one
  `S11_2_R14_TECHNICAL_RUNTIME_PROBE_GREEN` record.
- After the oneshot had become `inactive/dead`, systemd exposed an empty
  `InvocationID` through `systemctl show`.
- The controller consequently stopped with
  `S11_2_R14_PROBE_INVOCATION_RED` and exit status 2.

No second probe was started. No sample was deleted, rewritten, reclassified or
manually inserted. No S11 flag or acquisition/product boundary was changed.

## Root cause

The controller assumes that a completed short-lived oneshot retains its
`InvocationID` long enough to bind the post-run journal query. That assumption
does not hold on the target system. The probe itself is GREEN; the RED is a
post-execution evidence-binding contract failure.

Classification: `SYSTEMD_ONESHOT_INVOCATION_ID_LIFETIME_CONTRACT_BUG`

## Required recovery contract

Before any further runtime probe:

1. Reconcile the existing successful probe against the database using only
   aggregate, provenance-safe evidence and require exactly one valid R14
   technical sample.
2. Replace the post-exit `InvocationID` lookup with a journal cursor captured
   immediately before each unit start, then validate exactly one GREEN record
   after that cursor.
3. Run the full Application and Control test suites, secret/PII scan, CI and
   review; merge and freeze the repair before activation.
4. In a separately authorized backup-first R14.1 recovery, produce only the
   remaining samples required by the original minimum-five contract. If the
   existing sample cannot be proven valid, stop without modifying it.
5. Preserve the single-session, serial-execution, no-retry, no-REAL-sample and
   closed-product-boundary constraints.

R14.1 recovery was explicitly authorized on 2026-09-23. The runtime state
remains fail-closed until the repaired contract is reviewed, merged, frozen and
revalidated against the server before any further probe.

## Local validation note

The first repository-wide R14.1 validation run reported two simulator listener
failures because the paired temporary Application checkout lacked its required
Python 3.12 dependencies (`psycopg` was unavailable). No source or server state
caused that failure. After creating the repository-defined Python 3.12 test
environment, both affected simulator tests passed unchanged before the full
suite was repeated.

## Publishing note

The first branch push was rejected by GitHub privacy protection because the
unpublished local commit carried a protected private author address. No remote
ref was created. The local commit was amended without content changes to use
the project GitHub `noreply` identity before the branch was pushed again.
